course: dictionary
lesson: 12041
title: Circumference: the distance around
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Circumference is the distance all the way around the edge of a round shape. Imagine walking around the rim of a plate and counting every step: the total distance is the circumference. «Mia measured the circumference of the round pond with a long piece of string.» She laid the string around the edge, so the length of the string gave the circumference.
explain: Maths has a rule for finding circumference: C = pi x d, where d is the diameter, or C = 2 x pi x r, where r is the radius. Pi is about 3.14. «The ants walked slowly along the circumference of the plate.» The ants were walking along the edge, so circumference is the edge of a round area as well as its length.
fact: Circumference means the distance all the way around a circle.
fact: Circumference is another word for the perimeter of a circle.
fact: The circumference formula uses pi, which is about 3.14.
fact: «Circumference» can also mean the distance around anything round, like «the circumference of a tree trunk».
fact: The Earth's circumference is about 40,000 km, so it is the distance all the way around the planet.
exercise: «Mia measured the circumference of the round pond with a long piece of string.» What is the circumference of the pond? | The depth of the water in the middle | The number of ducks around it | *The distance all the way around the edge of the pond | The area of the pond's surface
exercise: «The ants walked slowly along the circumference of the plate.» Where were the ants walking? | Under the table | Inside the cupboard | In the middle of the plate | *Along the edge of the plate
exercise: A circle has a diameter of 10 cm and pi is about 3.14. Which formula finds the circumference? | *C = pi x d | C = pi + d | C = d squared | C = 10 divided by 2
test: «Leo wrapped a tape around the trunk to find its circumference.» What does circumference mean here? | The height of the trunk | The weight of the tree | *The distance around the trunk | The colour of the bark
test: Which phrase means finding the distance around a circle? | Paint the centre | *Find the circumference | Count the leaves | Draw a square
exam: Ruby says, «The circumference of the wheel is about 2 metres.» What does she mean? | The colour of the tyre | *The distance all the way around the wheel | The weight of the wheel | The distance across the middle of the wheel
